# UAT app versioning & in-app updates

## Version scheme (UAT → same model later for production)

Format: `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` + Android `versionCode` (always increases).

| When | Bump | Example |
|------|------|---------|
| Day-to-day / meaningful UAT ship | **patch** (last number) | `2.1.0` → `2.1.1` → `2.1.2` |
| User says build is **stable** / ready to stabilize the minor line | **minor** (middle number); patch resets to 0 | `2.1.7` → `2.2.0` |
| Breaking / major product line (rare; user must say so) | **major** | `2.x.y` → `3.0.0` |

**Never** bump minor or major unless the user explicitly asks to stabilize or start a new major line.

## Source of truth

- `eravat-app/version.json` — versionName, versionCode, changes[]
- `eravat-app/CHANGELOG.md` — human history
- Generated: `eravat-app/src/version.meta.ts` (via `npm run version:sync`)

## Before any meaningful UAT ship that installed apps should receive

1. **Ask the user** whether this work should be published to **installed UAT Android apps** (Settings → Update), unless they already said so.
2. If **yes**, bump with change notes (default **patch** unless they asked to stabilize → **minor**):

```bash
cd eravat-app
npm run version:bump -- patch "Short change 1" "Short change 2"
# stabilize: npm run version:bump -- minor "Stable UAT line 2.2" "…"
```

3. Then commit, push `uat`, and ensure CI can publish APK + `latest.json` (`UAT_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE`, or the existing `STAGE_SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE`, required for in-app Update).
4. If **no** (code-only / WIP / web-only), push or commit without `version:bump` — installed APKs stay on their current version.

## Stable UAT APK link (hard rule)

The share/install link is always this one object on UAT (`ttjtyvxfiqhjdngkgdkf`), bucket `app-updates`, path `staging/eravat-staging.apk`. Publishing overwrites it. The URL never changes, and it must be the file people install.

That object path keeps the historical `staging` segment on purpose. Installed apps and `https://tinyurl.com/23j8pezk` already point at it. Renaming this environment to UAT does not require an app release, and must not move or rename that object.

`https://ttjtyvxfiqhjdngkgdkf.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/app-updates/staging/eravat-staging.apk`

Short share link (301 to that URL): `https://tinyurl.com/23j8pezk`

Whenever a version is bumped **and** published to installed UAT apps:

1. Publish must `upsert` that exact object. Do not hand out a versioned APK filename.
2. `latest.json` `apkUrl` must stay that same URL, with the new `versionName` / `versionCode`.
3. Before sharing the link, confirm `latest.json` matches the bump. Then give the stable URL (and the short link). It already contains the new APK.

## Rules

- Never bump version or publish an APK update without user confirmation (or an explicit “push update to UAT apps” / “release 2.1.0” ask).
- Never hand-edit `src/version.meta.ts` — use `version:bump` / `version:sync`.
- versionCode must always increase; include real change bullets for testers.
- First install of a line needs a shell APK once; later patch/minor ships go through Settings → Update after bump + CI.
- Production will follow this same patch/minor stabilize model when that channel is set up.
